<title>GERMANY: Hesse Sept CPI down 0.1 pct, up 1.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Hesse Sept CPI down 0.1 pct, up 1.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state statistics office in the German state of Hesse reported the following consumer price changes for September.</p>
<p>    Cost of living		September	   August</p>
<p>    Month/month (pct change)  -0.1		  -0.1</p>
<p>    Year/year		     +1.2		  +1.2</p>
<p>NOTE - This data is later combined with data from three other major German states to calculate the preliminary figure for the whole of west Germany.</p>
<p>Hesse gave the following breakdown of its September cost of living data :</p>
<p>						 Percentage change</p>
<p> Index/component			   mth/mth   yr/yr    Index</p>
<p> Overall price index		     -0.1     + 1.2    114.1</p>
<p> Price index excl seasonal food	+0.1     +1.2     114.7</p>
<p> Price index excl heating oil, fuel  -0.2     +0.9     114.0</p>
<p> Rents					 +0.4     +2.9     126.2</p>
<p> Household energy			  +2.2     +0.2     100.0</p>
<p> Personal goods, services and other  -3.3     +0.7     123.7</p>
<p> Transport and communications	  +0.1     +1.3     114.6</p>
<p> Furniture and other household goods +0.1     +0.9     111.0</p>
<p> Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	   -0.2     +0.3     109.0</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes			   +0.1     +0.7     108.3</p>
<p> Health and personal care items	+0.1     +0.8     110.9</p>
<p> Education, entertainment, leisure   +0.5     +0.8     111.3</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
